{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/84806-starting-scion-looking-for-help","id":84806,"title":"Starting Scion - Looking for help","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","Scion"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-03-05T13:23:58-08:00","id":84806,"title":"Starting Scion - Looking for help","content":"Hey everyone! I know I'm kinda late to the party with the re-write of Scion coming out end of summer 2014, none-the-less my gaming group is really interested in trying the system out. We need some character creation clarification. We're having the most trouble with Birthrights, Purviews, and Boons. Can someone clarify how these work? Specifically, can I only access purviews that are granted to me by my birthrights (meaning I can only get new purviews by getting new birthrights by roleplaying)? Do I have &quot;dots&quot; in purviews or just dots in boons? We are finding it very challenging to learn this game, but we are sticking with it! Thanks in advance for your replies!<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2437-biodermcq","name":"biodermcq","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T13:59:40-08:00","id":84827,"title":"","content":"OK. First off, you are correct about the birthrights- you need a birthright to access a purview as a Hero. That can change for some things later on as a Demigod or God, but don't worry about that for now. Each dot spent on a birthright (specifically a Relic) can give access to a single purview. Once you have access, you can learn to use whatever boon you like. This is how it works for the &quot;All-Purpose Purviews&quot; (Health, Sky, Chaos, etc.) and the three &quot;Special Purviews&quot; (Magic, Mystery and Prophecy). The &quot;Pantheon-Specific Purviews&quot; do not need a relic to access- any Scion of that pantheon can access it, and it cannot be accessed by any other Scion. So, a Scion of Isis could access the Heku purview, but not Cheval or Iztli.<br /> <br /> Also, remember that a Scion is not limited to the purviews his divine parent favors (except for the pantheon specific purviews, that is). There is no reason our Scion of Isis can't start play with a relic granting access to the War or Darkness purviews, even though Isis doesn't favor them.<br /> <br /> As for the &quot;dots&quot; in purviews and boons, that works differently for the different kinds of purviews. I will explain each separately, starting with the pantheon specific purviews because that is the simplest.<br /> <br /> To purchase a pantheon specific purview, you must purchase each level in order. So, for the aforementioned Scion of Isis, you would start with Ren Harvest (Heku 1), then Sekem Blaze (Heku 2), then Sekem Barrier (Heku 3). You cannot buy a higher level power without purchasing the lower level powers first.<br /> <br /> All-Purpose Purviews are different. You do not buy levels in the purview; instead, you purchase each individual boon that you wish the character to have. Say the aforementioned Scion of Isis wanted to purchase powers of the Health purview. First, she would need a relic (either from character creation or one acquired during RP) to grant access to the purview. Once she has access, you can purchase for her whichever powers you wish, at any level you qualify for. To clarify, a Scion can only purchase boons, purviews or epic attributes at a level of his/her Legend -1. So, a Scion with Legend 2 could only purchase 1st level powers, while a Scion with Legend 4 could purchase powers of up to level 3. So, our Scion of Isis could purchase Assess Health (Health 1), then purchase Heal/Infect (Health 3), without also having to purchase Blessing of Health/Curse of Frailty (Health 3). Just remember that, even though you can pick and choose which powers you want to buy, it's not always smart to skip every power to get the one you want. For example, I wouldn't be comfortable using any Fire boons unless I first bought Fire Immunity (Fire 1). ;-)<br /> <br /> Next we will discuss 2 of the special purviews, Mystery and Prophecy. Each of these purviews is bought one level at a time. Unlike the other purviews, there are no special powers for each different level. Buying higher levels simply gives more dice to the (Intelligence+Mystery) or (Intelligence+Prophecy) rolls to activate the powers.<br /> <br /> Lastly is the other special purview, Magic. Magic works like a combination of the other special purviews and the all-purpose purviews. You must buy the Magic purview one level at a time, and must buy the levels in order, just like Mystery and Prophecy. However, every time you buy a level, you get a spell of that level. For example, when you buy Magic 1, You can choose to learn the spell Ariadne's Thread, or the spell The Unlidded Eye. Once you have a level of Magic, you can buy additional spells for that level as if they were all-purpose boons. While you do need to buy each level of magic in order, you do not need to buy every spell of each level before purchasing the next level. So, let's take our Scion of Isis again. She starts by purchasing Magic 1, and chooses the spell Ariadne's Thread. When she has some more XP, she decides to buy Magic 2 and chooses the spell Bona Fortuna. Later, she decides that she would like The Unlidded Eye spell in her repertoire, and goes back to purchase that.<br /> <br /> I hope that helps you. If you have any more questions, I or one of the other helpful gamers at the forum would be more than happy to assist you. Happy adventuring!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1416,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","user":"NutiketAiel","date":".  Correcting Spell Name 03-05-2014, 05:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T14:09:21-08:00","id":84836,"title":"","content":"This makes things soooo clear (also, my Scion happens to be the Son of Isis, so your examples are perfect.) If I have more questions i will ask! Thanks so much for your help.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2437-biodermcq","name":"biodermcq","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-03-05T14:41:29-08:00","id":84857,"title":"","content":"Glad to do it. :-)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1416-nutiketaiel","name":"NutiketAiel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1416_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"303"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}